  "observations": [
    "The canonical Service no longer has one OnceLock Session initializer that would force initial telephone hosting to displace public AI hosting. A protected named registry is bounded by16 and the configured Connection limit. Duplicate names, capacity overflow and stopped runtime registration are refused. Cancellation/drain permanently close registration under its mutex before snapshotting all hosts. Queued snapshots recheck closure under the work mutex so shutdown cannot lose late work. A controlled third fixture pauses after the open snapshot, closes hosts, then releases the caller and verifies the work set stays empty. Public Vapi installs under its explicit public-vapi key; no public installation/permission/model-execution command is added.",
    "Completed Session metadata is cloned to each independently configured host. One bounded Runtime task owns its child notification JoinSet; failed or blocked admission cannot prevent a different host from being polled. Dropping that parent aborts/owns its child futures rather than detaching notifications. The notification itself carries no retained command reader or IO grant. Each host must independently recheck exact target/current source authority and deduplicate logical work.",
    "Cancellation reaches every registered host before parallel draining starts. All drains are joined even when one returns cleanup uncertainty; the first captured error is returned only after the others finish. Registrations are retained so existing owned host handles remain available for another drain. The failure fixture verifies both independent hosts receive exact original credential/operation metadata and both drain despite one failing.",
    "Actual signed/HTTP public hosting, strict/missing-context/missing-profile refusal, TOML discovery/revocation/ambiguity, exact ACK/multiple native audio frames, duplicate creation/export suppression and provider shutdown remain verified in the9existing fixtures. The public Session and private AI caller/context/return/restart regressions also pass. The prior private one-frame incident remains causally unestablished; this does not qualify clean general provider availability.",
    "This is a coexistence prerequisite for G6-044 initial telephone integration, not an implemented initial telephone adapter or migrated public call workflow. The existing initial-call gap is explicit: SIP guarded media contexts are currently tied to DeviceReplacementPreparation; generic PreparedOutboundConnection.commit refuses Sessions with checked participant controllers, and checked staged admission currently accepts physical native peers. Initial SIP needs its own current endpoint/admission custody, not a fabricated replacement/source ticket or an unguarded legacy join."
  ],
